# Before You Design / Decide / Implement

**Source of truth:** `PRIVATE SECURITY SERVICES MANAGEMENT SYSTEM DESIGN.docx`  
(Company: HIGHLINK Investigation and Security Guard Company Limited — PSSMS)

You already have foundation APIs/backend; many features are still incomplete. **Do not invent product scope.** Finish or extend only what the design document requires.

## Pre-flight checklist (every task)

1. **Which of the 29 modules?** (see `pssms-modules.mdc`) — name it before coding.
2. **Which portal/app/account?** (see `pssms-portals-and-accounts.mdc`) — portal ≠ microservice.
3. **Who creates / reviews / approves?** (see `pssms-roles-authority.mdc`) — creator ≠ approver.
4. **Data separation?** Guards ≠ customer employees ≠ visitors ≠ suppliers ≠ other security companies.
5. **Device/channel?** Fingerprint, face, GPS, QR, NFC, RFID, ANPR, CCTV metadata, SMS/WhatsApp — see `pssms-devices-and-channels.mdc`.
6. **Does it control, record, automate, verify, or report — with audit?** If only UI chrome, stop.

```text
❌ New silo app / duplicate attendance table / approve own request / Nest streaming CCTV video
✅ Domain lib + shared approvals + RLS tenant keys + events/metadata + audit trail
```

## Product in one sentence

One **integrated enterprise platform** that controls, records, automates, verifies, and reports **all** private security company operations nationwide — modular, secure, scalable, auditable.

## When unsure

Re-read the matching section in the design docx (modules §3–34, portals §35, accounts §36, design principles §37) before proposing architecture or writing code.
